@startuml "Facade - Checkout (Homework) - Class Diagram"
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
title Facade — homework 1, and what it owes you on partial failure


class CheckoutFacade <<Facade>> {
  + placeOrder(customer, sku, qty, amount, address) : OrderResult
}
class OrderResult <<record>>

class InventoryService
class PaymentService
class ShippingService
class ReceiptService

CheckoutFacade ..> InventoryService
CheckoutFacade ..> PaymentService
CheckoutFacade ..> ShippingService
CheckoutFacade ..> ReceiptService
CheckoutFacade ..> OrderResult

note right of CheckoutFacade
  Reserve, charge, book, receipt.
  One call, four subsystems.
end note

note as N1
  <b>The exercise is partial failure.</b>

  Stock is reserved, then the payment is
  declined. Somebody must put it back — and
  if the facade does not, every caller needs
  the subsystem knowledge the facade exists
  to remove.

  So compensation lives here. A facade over
  several subsystems <b>inherits responsibility
  for half-finished work</b>.
end note

@enduml
